tune, so the series of partials may be taken as about ·75, 1·90, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, &c., all the upper notes being brought into tune by ¶ modifications in the form of the bell in a good instrument.' The length of the French horn varies with the 'crook' which determines its pitch. @@FN@@
