===
The following contains the length in English inches for each crook, as given by Mr. Blaikley: *B*♭ (alto) 108, *A*♮ 114½, *A*♭ 121½, *G* 128¾, *F* 144½, *E*♮ 153, *E*♭ 162, *D*♮ 171½, *C* 192¾, *B*♭ (basso) 216¾, hence the length varies from 9 ft. to 18 ft. ¾ inch. @@FN@@
>>>
<<<
@@FN@@
===
By a curious error in all the German editions, Zamminer is said to make the length of the *E*♭ Waldhorn 27 feet, or the length of the wave of the *lowest* note, in place of his 13·4 feet. Zamminer, however, says that the instrument is named from the *Octave above* the lowest note, @@FN@@
>>>
<<<
@@FN@@
===
and that hence the wave-length of *this Octave* is the length of the horn.—*Translator.*]

